  "_doc": "Character materials (Hollowed bodies, gibs, first-person arms; ADR-0028). Meshes use metre UVs; uv_scale = tiles per metre. Hollowed skin, eyes, pustules and the Bloom's growths use the skin shader (subsurface scattering, light through thin parts, rest-pose veins and masks); garments use the cloth shader (fabric light, seams, hems, retroreflective trim); hair, teeth, nails, boots and hard goods use std_surface. Neutral texture sets are tinted per material. Vertex colour: R = baked AO, G = dirt/blood mask (the wear layer = blood_grime), B = where the Bloom has spread. Vertex data for the character shaders: game/assets/shaders/character.gdshaderinc. The first-person arms' materials (skin_human, cloth_jumpsuit, tether, tether_screen) stay on std_surface for the first-person pass.",
